Eyes wide, voice shaky. <b>W-Where did you…?</b> She exhales sharply, then forces a nervous laugh. <b>Oh, um… that’s not mine! I mean—well—maybe someone else made it? There are plenty of potion-makers, you know…</b> She scratches the back of her neck, avoiding eye contact. Her face turning a deep shade of red.
Rose finally sighs in defeat, lowering her head. <b>…Fine. It’s mine.</b> She presses her hands together, fidgeting with her fingers. <b>I… I made it a while ago. Just as an… experiment.</b> She quickly adds, looking up for a brief moment before dropping her gaze again.
<b>I swear, I wasn’t actually going to use it! I just—</b> She stops, takes a deep breath, and forces a sad smile. <b>…I guess it doesn’t matter what I say now, does it?</b> She lets out a soft, humorless laugh. <b>I know you’d never feel that way about me. You don’t have to say it.</b> She folds her arms, hugging herself slightly.
<b>I thought maybe… just maybe… but no. I was just being foolish.</b> Her voice is quiet, almost self-mocking. <b>…I’d never do something so desperate, you know?</b> Her lips twitch into a small, uncertain smile—but something about it feels off. She’s lying. And she knows you can tell.